  "question": {
    "text": "The potential energy of a $1 \\mathrm{~kg}$ particle free move along the $\\mathrm{x}$-axis is given by\n$$\nV(x)=\\left(\\frac{x^4}{4}-\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right) J\n$$\nThe total mechanical energy of the particle $2 \\mathrm{~J}$. Then, the maximum speed (in $\\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$ ) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "v9T32",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GUzfa",
      "text": "\n$3 / \\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "vpzFu",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8978a",
      "text": "\n$1 / \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{k} \\mathrm{E}_{\\max }=\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{T}}-\\mathrm{U}_{\\min }$\n$\\mathrm{U}_{\\min }(\\pm 1)=-1 / 4 \\mathrm{~J}$\n$\\mathrm{KE}_{\\max }=9 / 4 \\mathrm{~J} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{U}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\mathrm{~J}$",
    "image": null
  },
